post_install() {
  # A pacman scriptlet runs as root and cannot touch a user's systemd manager,
  # so the two per-session steps are told, not done. A reboot does both.
  cat <<'MSG'
vcamd: the daemon is installed and its socket is enabled for every user.

Reboot, and it is ready. Without rebooting, this session needs both halves
picked up by hand:

  1. The module:  sudo modprobe v4l2loopback
  2. The socket:  systemctl --user daemon-reload &&
                  systemctl --user start vcamd.socket

Then add the bar widget and start a capture:

  omarchy plugin add https://github.com/Sphiment/omavcamd.git --enable
  vcamd start

Nothing needs root again after this: the module is configured at install time
because a `systemd --user` service cannot load one.
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MSG'
vcamd: restart the daemon to run the new binary:
  systemctl --user restart vcamd.socket vcamd.service
If the module parameters changed, the new nodes appear after a reboot.
MSG
}

post_remove() {
  # The file that loads this module at boot goes with the package, so an
  # uninstall should not leave it loaded either. v4l2loopback-dkms stays
  # installed and is shared with other tools, so the unload is best effort:
  # a module something is actually using has a non-zero refcount and
  # `modprobe -r` refuses it, which is the behaviour we want.
  # The units are gone with the package, but a session that already started
  # them keeps its copies until it is told otherwise.
  # `disable` would be wrong twice over: the enablement was a symlink in
  # /usr/lib that went with the package, and vcamd.service has no [Install]
  # at all — it exists to be socket-activated.
  cat <<'MSG'
vcamd: stop what is left of this login session with
  systemctl --user stop vcamd.socket vcamd.service
MSG
  modprobe -r v4l2loopback 2>/dev/null || cat <<'MSG'
vcamd: v4l2loopback is still loaded because something is using it, and was
left alone. Nothing vcamd installed loads it any more; another package's
configuration, if there is one, still will.
MSG
}
